Package: mediamtx
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: systemd
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/bluenviron/mediamtx
Description: MediaMTX Streaming Server - RTSP/RTMP/HLS/WebRTC/SRT relay
 MediaMTX is a self-hosted, dependency-free media streaming server written
 in Go. A single binary serves RTSP, RTMP, HLS, WebRTC and SRT at the same
 time: cameras and encoders publish a stream once, and any number of players
 pull it over the protocol of their choice. It is a natural relay/base for
 IP camera monitoring and live broadcasting on a NAS.
 .
 A built-in status console opens in a new browser tab from the TOS desktop
 route /mediamtx/: it lists the active paths, links to the HLS player page
 and proxies the complete management API. The management API (9997), metrics
 (9998) and playback (9996) listeners are bound to loopback only and are
 reachable exclusively through the TOS web server gateway.
 .
 Media ports are opened for LAN clients because they are the core function:
 RTSP 8554, RTMP 1935, HLS 8888, WebRTC 8889 (UDP/ICE 8189), SRT 8890.
 Anonymous readers are allowed; publishing requires the credentials generated
 at install time and stored root-readable in
 /var/lib/mediamtx/publisher_password.txt.
 .
 Configuration lives in /var/lib/mediamtx/mediamtx.yml and is hot-reloaded.
 Recordings and configuration are kept in /var/lib/mediamtx: 'apt remove'
 keeps them, 'apt purge' deletes them. The service runs as a dedicated
 unprivileged user in a hardened systemd sandbox.
 .
 Upstream: https://github.com/bluenviron/mediamtx (MIT)
 Upstream author: bluenviron. Packaged for TOS by the deb Maintainer.
